# qmldir — explicit module manifest for quickshell/modules/screensaver/
# (quick task 260827-b52). Mirrors every sibling module manifest's own
# standing instruction (see modules/lock/qmldir, modules/osd/qmldir): any
# .qml type added to this directory that is NOT declared below becomes
# unresolvable to `shell.qml`'s `import "modules/screensaver"` —
# qml-import-check enforces this. Any FUTURE type added to this directory
# MUST do the same, in the same commit that creates it.
#
# Screensaver is NOT a singleton — shell.qml mounts one ordinary,
# always-on Scope at shell root, which fans out to one
# ScreensaverSurface per screen through its own Variants (ruling D5).
#
# SaverTerminal/SaverAurora/SaverConstellation/SaverRail are the four
# operator-picked styles, selected by ScreensaverSurface.qml's own
# `style` switch. Every one must be declared here the same commit it
# gains a `case` arm in that switch, or the arm references an
# unresolvable type. The fifth valid style value, "off", has no file and
# no arm: it is handled upstream in Screensaver.qml's `inhibited`, which
# never mounts a surface at all.
module qs.modules.screensaver
Screensaver 1.0 Screensaver.qml
ScreensaverSurface 1.0 ScreensaverSurface.qml
SaverArt 1.0 SaverArt.qml
SaverTerminal 1.0 SaverTerminal.qml
SaverAurora 1.0 SaverAurora.qml
SaverConstellation 1.0 SaverConstellation.qml
SaverRail 1.0 SaverRail.qml
